# 035 - the comparisons that succeed: == and != on two values of the same type,
# `nil == nil` is true, and Str orders byte-lexicographically, so "ab" < "b"
# (§6/.40). Prefixes sort before the longer string they prefix.
--- source
print 1 == 1;
print 1 != 2;
print nil == nil;
print true == false;
print "a" == "a";
print "a" < "b";
print "ab" < "b";
print 2 <= 2;
print 3 >= 4;
--- expect
true
true
true
false
true
true
true
true
false
